---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const { name } = SITE;
const { legalName, email, jurisdiction } = SITE.business;
---

<Policy title="Terms of Service" description={`Terms for buying and using ${name}.`}>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you buy or use {name} (the “extension”) and this website, provided by <strong>{legalName}</strong> (“we”, “us”).
    By buying or using {name}, you agree to them.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Pre-order and delivery</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      During the early-bird period, {name} is sold as a <strong>pre-order</strong>. The extension is still being built when you pay.
    </li>
    <li>We will email you a license key and access to the beta version within <strong>{SITE.deliveryDays} days</strong> of your purchase.</li>
    <li>
      If we don’t deliver within that time, you can choose to wait or get a full refund. See the <a href="/refund">Refund Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Beta versions may have bugs. We will fix reported problems as quickly as we reasonably can.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Your license</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your purchase gives you a <strong>lifetime, non-exclusive, non-transferable license</strong> to use {name} for personal or business purposes,
      in up to <strong>{SITE.devicesPerLicense} browsers</strong> at a time.
    </li>
    <li>“Lifetime” means for as long as we offer the product. It includes the updates we release for it.</li>
    <li>
      You may not share, resell or publish your license key, or copy, modify, reverse-engineer or redistribute the extension, except where the law
      allows it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Free trial</h2>
  <p>
    The extension may let you process a limited number of files (currently {SITE.trialFiles}) before a license key is required. The trial can change.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use {name} only with email accounts you are allowed to access.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Check the results.</strong> {name} reads invoices automatically and can make mistakes, especially with unusual layouts, scanned
      documents or password-protected files. You are responsible for reviewing exported files and figures before relying on them.
    </li>
    <li>Keep your own copies of important documents. {name} does not change or delete your emails.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Not financial or tax advice</h2>
  <p>
    {name} is a file organising tool. It does not provide accounting, tax or legal advice. Talk to a qualified professional for that.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    {name} works inside Gmail, which is provided by Google. We are not affiliated with or endorsed by Google. Changes Google makes to Gmail may
    temporarily affect how the extension works; we will work to restore compatibility, but cannot guarantee uninterrupted service.
    Payments are processed by Dodo Payments under its own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Warranty disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    Apart from the refund rights in our <a href="/refund">Refund Policy</a> and any rights you have by law that can’t be excluded, {name} is
    provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, including fitness for a particular purpose and accuracy of extracted data.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses (such as lost profits, penalties, or missed filing
    deadlines), and our total liability for any claim is limited to the amount you paid for {name}.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Ending the license</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using {name} at any time. We may deactivate a license that is shared, resold or used to break these terms. If we deactivate it
    for any other reason, we will refund what you paid.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. We will change the date at the top and, for significant changes, email customers. Changes never reduce what you
    already paid for.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. Courts in {jurisdiction} have jurisdiction, without affecting consumer rights you have where you live.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</p>
</Policy>
